  "fixedRule": [
    "Retain existing worker count, group partitioning, count lead and source prefetch window.",
    "Admit parser groups in index order only; atomically reserve their validated estimated uncompressed source bytes before loading/dispatch.",
    "At each completed result atomically replace its reservation with exact owned backing-buffer bytes; borrowed content contributes zero owned bytes and retains its existing consume acknowledgment.",
    "Retain exact owned bytes until the ordered sink callback settles.",
    "Admit only when owned plus reserved plus next estimate fits; admit one indivisible oversized group exclusively when all prior groups have drained and charged bytes are zero.",
    "Allow completion of already admitted parses whose encoded output exceeds estimates; stop further admission until drain.",
    "Wake waiters on admission, result replacement, sink progress and terminal failure; preserve existing 25 ms cancellation polling and callback drain."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This bounds admission estimates, not complete process memory or WASM heap capacity.",
    "It does not change parser worker count, grouping, compression workers, OPFS reservation or source prefetch limits.",
    "Any throughput/memory comparison must be fresh full-import qualification; no performance claim is made from these source changes or unit tests.",
    "The policy is fixed before new timing; no per-corpus tuning or outcome-dependent adjustment."
